+# Code changes for the Oct 22 decisions
+
+Base: `main` at `44e7b89` (scaffold + docs + offline fix). Owners per the Oct 22 role split. Every change
+is additive to the contracts so the four workstreams can proceed in parallel; `packages/schemas` v0.2 is
+the shared contract and lands first (this commit).
+
+## Design rules these changes implement
+
+1. **Schedule on play-time, display match clock.** Every event and packet carries `play_ms` (monotonic from
+   first kickoff, no stoppage time ambiguity) and `{period, clock_ms}` for display. All interval arithmetic
+   uses `play_ms`.
+2. **The gate is mandatory and structural.** AI-written text reaches a screen only inside an `OverlayPacket`
+   that carries `approval_id`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`. The renderer refuses packets without them.
+   There is no auto-approve path in the API. The SLA timer holds, never approves.
+3. **Cues are code, captions are AI.** The deaf-fan strike cue (`FanCue`) is deterministic, contains no
+   generated text, and is published immediately on `shot_taken` (≤ 1 s). The caption (`FanCard`) is
+   generated text and is published only after the operator's decision on the matching proposal.
+4. **Scheduling is code, content is AI.** The producer agent proposes layer, line, and payload; the
+   `scheduler` module (plain Python) assigns `t_in/t_out`, resolves collisions, applies the one-story-per-
+   window rule and goal/red-card preemption, and computes `hold_advice` from `pressure_trend`.
+5. **Model choice is visible.** Three router deployments (`router-quality`, `router-balanced`,
+   `router-cost`); each agent is bound to one; the served model from `response.model` is written to the
+   span and to the output record (`model_served`).
+
+## By workstream
+
+### Shared contract — `packages/schemas` (this commit; review Thu AM)
+
+- `MatchEvent`: `play_ms`, `phase_id`, `stoppage_id`; new `EventType` values `shot_taken`, `stoppage`,
+  `whistle`, `crowd`; documented `attrs` keys (`assist_by`, `key_pass`, `blocker`, `reason`, `restart`,
+  `crowd_level`).
+- `MatchState`: `shots` ledger (`ShotRecord` with `chance_rank`), `xg_last_5min`, `shots_last_5min`,
+  `pressure_trend`, `momentum_label`, `last_stoppage`, `current_phase`, `recap_points`.
+- `Moment`: `play_ms`, `beat` (`chance` | `result` | `none`).
+- `Explanation`, `NarrativeVariant`, `OverlayProposal`: `model_served`, `routing` (which router deployment).
+- `OverlayProposal`: scheduler fields (`cue_id`, `t_in_ms`, `t_out_ms`, `priority`, `replaces`,
+  `min_hold_ms`, `max_delay_ms`), `evidence` (readable lines), `alternatives`, `hold_advice`.
+- `OverlayPacket` (replaces `OverlayItem`): adds required approval fields, `profile`, `verified`,
+  `fallback`; `OverlayLayer` adds `caption`, `player_tag`, `pitch_overlay`.
+- `FanCue`, `FanCard`: the deaf-fan records. `Persona` = `fan | deaf | analyst`. `Lang` = `en | es | hi`.
+- `DecisionAction` adds `reject`; `DecisionLogEntry` unchanged otherwise.
+- `RecapRequest` / `Recap` for the catch-up card.
+
+### Data pipeline — Pranav (`services/simulator`, `services/ingest`) — reference match Thu EOD
+
+Simulator (`engine.py`): maintain `play_ms` across periods; emit `shot_taken` 400–900 ms before `shot`
+(same `phase_id`, carry `xg` on both); emit `stoppage` + `whistle` for fouls, cards, half/full time, goals,
+ball out (reason, against, restart, restart coordinates); assign `phase_id` per possession; set `assist_by`
+and mark `key_pass`; set `blocker` on blocked shots; emit `crowd` with `crowd_level` derived from xG,
+goals, stoppages; add rare seeded `offside` and `var_review` stoppage reasons; write the reference match
+to `data/reference/match-042.jsonl` and un-ignore that folder. Calibration targets unchanged (see
+`tests/test_engine.py`); add assertions for the new event counts.
+
+State engine (`stats.py`): fill the new `MatchState` fields; raise the big chance as two moments
+(`beat=chance` on `shot_taken`, `beat=result` on `shot`); zone namer `zone(x, y)`; `pressure_trend` over
+the last 3 minutes; `momentum_label`; `recap(last_n_min)` returning `Recap`; `recap_points` from moments
+with importance ≥ 0.6. Add `tests/test_stats.py` cases for each.
+
+Evaluation dataset: `evals/datasets/reference-042.jsonl` (moments + ground-truth answers to the persona
+questions) and `evals/datasets/planted-falsehoods.jsonl` (N lines with one wrong number/name each).
+
+### Agents and evaluations — Siranjeevi (`services/agents`, `evals`)
+
+- `config.py`: `ROUTER_QUALITY`, `ROUTER_BALANCED`, `ROUTER_COST` deployment names; map explainer and
+  producer → quality, narrator → balanced, personalizer → cost.
+- `clients.py`: one `OpenAIChatClient` per router deployment; wrap `agent.run` to read `response.model`
+  into `model_served`, set span attributes `crq.agent`, `crq.routing`, `crq.model_served`.
+- `scheduler.py` (new, pure code): `schedule(proposal, on_air, state) -> proposal` implementing collision
+  avoidance per layer, earliest free gap, one-story-per-window (30 s), goal/red-card preemption of the
+  lower third, `min_hold_ms`, per-kind `max_delay_ms`, and `hold_advice` when `pressure_trend == rising`
+  and the proposal is not a goal. Unit tests with hand-built on-air lists.
+- `workflow.py`: run `scheduler.schedule` after the producer; build `FanCue` from the chance-beat moment
+  without any model call; build `FanCard` from the result-beat variant for persona `deaf`; drop
+  `squad_author` from the pipeline (file stays); personas `fan | deaf | analyst`; languages `en es hi`.
+- `prompts/`: personalizer gets the `deaf` register (plain words, where on the pitch, who, score after;
+  no sound references); producer prompt no longer decides timing (scheduler does) and must return
+  `alternatives` (the graphic it rejected and why); explainer unchanged.
+- Agent Service: `register_agents.py` creates/updates the four agents by name in the Foundry project
+  (`azure-ai-projects`), so they are inspectable in the portal; the runner still executes locally via
+  Agent Framework.
+- `evals/run_eval.py`: replay the reference match offline, collect (moment, explanation, line, variants),
+  submit a Foundry evaluation run (groundedness, relevance, fluency per language), run the planted-
+  falsehood set through the pipeline and count catches, write `evals/results/latest.md` in the README
+  table format. Nightly job in `.github/workflows/evals.yml`.
+
+### API — Swami, with Mudassar on the contract (`services/api`)
+
+- Replace `OverlayItem` with `OverlayPacket`; `_decide` stamps `approval_id/approved_by/approved_at` from
+  the decision; `POST /proposals/{id}/reject`; SLA timer path unchanged (holds, logs actor `sla-timer`).
+- Publish `FanCue` on chance-beat moments immediately to `/ws/viewer?persona=deaf` and the overlay hub;
+  publish `FanCard` only inside the packet after approval/override.
+- `GET /recap?minutes=10|20|30` → `Recap`; `GET /decisions.csv` download; `GET /schedule` (what is on
+  each layer and queued) for the console.
+- Match clock vs play-time: the replay loop advances `play_ms`; WebSocket `state` messages carry both.
+
+### Front end — Mudassar (`web`) — per `frontend/decisions-2026-10-22.md`
+
+Renderer holds the clock and schedules on `t_in_ms/t_out_ms`; upsert by `cue_id`; `replaces[]`; caption
+layer never queues; refuse any packet lacking approval fields; approve / hold / reject + undo-as-revert
+Friday, edit-with-re-verify Saturday; deaf-fan view with the pulse-edge cue and caption; catch-up card
+calling `/recap`; scheduler view (layers × time) on the console.
+
+### Azure plumbing — Swami (`infra`)
+
+- `ai.bicep`: three router deployments with `routing.mode` quality/balanced/cost; remove the Speech
+  resource (dropped scope); keep `gpt-4.1-mini` as fallback.
+- `apps.bicep`: env vars `ROUTER_QUALITY`, `ROUTER_BALANCED`, `ROUTER_COST`.
+- Logic App for the SLA hold (Cosmos change feed → 20 s → `POST /proposals/{id}/hold` as `sla-timer`).
+- First `azd up` will surface API-version drift on the Foundry account and deployments; fix in place.
+
+### Docs and README — Swami (Sunday)
+
+README top section: live URL, video, eval table, planted-falsehood result, test count, synthetic-data
+section with calibration numbers, judge walkthrough, limits, operator quote. SOLUTION/DESIGN/ARCHITECTURE
+updated to the rules above; PLAN roles updated.
+
+## Order of landing
+
+1. Schemas v0.2 (this commit) → 15-min review Thu AM.
+2. Pranav: simulator events + reference match (Thu EOD). Siranjeevi: scheduler + router clients (Thu).
+   Mudassar: renderer on the new packet (Thu). Swami: `azd up`, router deployments (Thu).
+3. Fri: API wiring, FanCue/FanCard, end-to-end demo.
+4. Sat: hold advice (if slipped), catch-up card, edit-with-re-verify, Agent Service registration, evals.
+5. Sun: README, docs, parked items. Mon: video, pitch, project page. Tue: submit.
